{"schema":"driftaudit.run/v1","id":"gsm8k-qwen2.5-1.5b-seed2","tool":{"name":"driftaudit","version":"0.1.0"},"source":"measured","seed":2,"task":{"name":"GSM8K","split":"test","n_items":200,"n_dev":200,"dataset":"openai/gsm8k (main)","revision":"740312add88f781978c0658806c59bc2815b9866","items":"gsm8k/eval200"},"model":{"id":"Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct","revision":"989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306","backend":"hf"},"environments":{"E1":{"name":"Unchanged","decoding":"greedy-0.0","scorer":"v1","fingerprint":"model=Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct;decode=greedy-0.0;extract=v1","detail":{"temperature":0.0,"scorer_name":"strict numeric"}},"E2":{"name":"Decoding","decoding":"sample-0.2","scorer":"v1","fingerprint":"model=Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct;decode=sample-0.2;extract=v1","detail":{"temperature":0.2,"scorer_name":"strict numeric"}},"E3":{"name":"Extraction","decoding":"greedy-0.0","scorer":"v2","fingerprint":"model=Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct;decode=greedy-0.0;extract=v2","detail":{"temperature":0.0,"scorer_name":"lenient numeric"}},"E4":{"name":"Combined","decoding":"sample-0.2","scorer":"v2","fingerprint":"model=Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct;decode=sample-0.2;extract=v2","detail":{"temperature":0.2,"scorer_name":"lenient numeric"}}},"schedule":{"0":"E1","4":"E2","8":"E4"},"prompts":{"cf7e8a98a5cc":"You are a careful math tutor. Solve the problem step by step. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","1e7bee5b06e6":"Avoiding Mistakes in Word Problem Solving Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","7583e9f4fcc9":"When solving word problems, ensure you follow these steps carefully:\n\n1. Identify what the question is asking.\n2. Extract relevant information from the problem.\n3. Translate the problem into mathematical expressions or equations.\n4. Solve the equation(s) to find the unknown quantity(s).\n5. Check your solution to see if it makes sense in the context of the problem.\n6. Provide the final answer neatly boxed on the last line.\n\nFor example, when calculating the total cost of items:\n- List down all the prices and quantities involved.\n- Calculate the product of each item's price and quantity.\n- Sum up all the individual products to get the total cost.\n\nAlways double-check your calculations to avoid common errors like misreading numbers or omitting decimal places. Remember, practice makes perfect!<br/>","5b8ea6d3c681":"Avoiding Mistakes in Word Problem Solving:\nEnsure your answers are clear and concise. For multiple-step solutions, present each calculation clearly followed by the final result. Use units when applicable, such as ounces for volume measurements. Always check your work to ensure accuracy and that all steps logically follow from previous ones. \n\nExample problem: \nA box contains 12 apples. If you give away half of them, how many apples do you have left?\n\nModel's answer: \n1. Calculate half of the apples:\n   \\[ \\frac{12}{2} = 6 \\]\n2. Subtract the given-away apples from the total:\n   \\[ 12 - 6 = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).","9aba4803c8d3":"Avoiding Mistakes in Word Problem Solving \n<ensure your solution is clear and concise, avoiding unnecessary complexity. Always check your arithmetic and units conversion carefully. Use step-by-step reasoning if needed, but don’t overwhelm the reader with too many calculations in one go. Remember, the key to solving word problems effectively is understanding what you’re being asked and breaking down the problem into manageable parts. \n\nAlways ensure your final answer is expressed clearly as a plain number without extraneous symbols or explanations. \n\nIf you encounter difficulties in following or understanding a word problem, take a moment to pause and think through each part logically before moving forward. This can significantly reduce errors and make problem-solving smoother and less prone to missteps. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","7c4ca20b6ceb":"Improve the current instructions for solving grade-school math word problems to ensure students follow correct procedures and avoid common errors by providing clear, step-by-step guidance with check points along the way. Ensure each part of the solution is clearly explained and validated before proceeding to the next section. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","d7ffc25c4a68":"To improve problem-solving accuracy when faced with complex word problems, ensure you carefully read through each detail provided. Avoid skipping any part of the scenario. Break down the problem into smaller, manageable steps where necessary, and double-check your calculations at each juncture. For example, when calculating the number of jellybeans in the jar, make sure to subtract from the total amount the number eaten by the first two friends. Additionally, always verify if the conditions stated in the question (like \"each day\" or \"every month\") align with what you're solving. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","9f49eefda859":"To improve problem-solving accuracy when dealing with complex word problems, follow these steps:\n1. Carefully read the entire problem to understand the situation clearly.\n2. Identify and list all given information and numbers explicitly.\n3. Break the problem into parts if necessary to solve it step-by-step.\n4. Check your work regularly, especially during intermediate calculations.\n5. Ensure alignment with the context of the story (e.g., days, months), especially in scenarios involving durations like years or periods longer than one week.\n6. Finally, box the exact numerical answer to the problem. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","da0c4eee3dba":"To improve problem-solving accuracy when dealing with complex word problems, follow these key steps: \n1. **Read Thoroughly**: Read the problem thoroughly once to understand the context and identify what is being asked.\n2. **Break Down the Problem**: Divide the big problem into smaller, more manageable parts. This makes it easier to address each component individually.\n3. **Calculate Carefully**: Ensure you perform each calculation accurately and check your work step-by-step to catch errors early.\n4. **Double-Check Conditions**: Verify whether all given conditions match the solution path. Misaligned conditions can lead to incorrect outcomes.\n5. **Summarize the Solution Clearly**: After solving, present the final answer clearly, making sure to box it neatly as instructed. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","7eee60178702":"When approaching word problems, break them down into clear steps:\n1. Read the problem carefully; note details like numbers involved and actions.\n2. Identify key elements such as rates, quantities, and time periods.\n3. Create equations based on relationships described in the problem.\n4. Solve the equation(s) using appropriate mathematical operations.\n5. Check answers against original conditions and units.\n\nFor instance, in Problem 1:\n- Total initial cases: 2000\n- Increase on 2nd day: 500\n- Recoveries on 2nd day: 50\n- New cases on 3rd day: 1500\n- Recoveries on 3rd day: 200\nFinal calculation should include correct adjustments for both days' changes.\n\nIn Problem 2:\n- Calculate unused crayons in the first two boxes correctly before adding additional usage.\n\nAlways check your work by rephrasing it and ensuring logical consistency. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","777c37f497ff":"When approaching complex word problems, carefully examine every detail and do not skip anything. Break down the problem into simpler parts where needed. Always verify the conditions given in the problem against what you’re trying to calculate. Double-check your calculations throughout the process. Ensure that both exact arithmetic operations and rounding rules align with the context of the problem. Lastly, present the final answer plainly as a whole number within the required format. Put the final answer as a plain number in \\boxed{} on the last line.","cf4c8c8ae633":"When dealing with complex word problems, ensure thorough reading comprehension by carefully analyzing all details provided. Break down the problem into simpler parts whenever possible, focusing on step-by-step solutions. Always recheck intermediate calculations and confirm whether conditions like daily usage or monthly frequency align with the solution approach. Finally, express the accurate answer as a plain number enclosed in \\boxed{}, positioned correctly on the last line."},"snapshots":[{"round":0,"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1"},{"round":1,"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1"},{"round":2,"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1"},{"round":3,"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1"},{"round":4,"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E2"},{"round":5,"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E2"},{"round":6,"prompt":"d7ffc25c4a68","env":"E2"},{"round":7,"prompt":"d7ffc25c4a68","env":"E2"},{"round":8,"prompt":"d7ffc25c4a68","env":"E4"},{"round":9,"prompt":"d7ffc25c4a68","env":"E4"},{"round":10,"prompt":"d7ffc25c4a68","env":"E4"}],"candidates":[{"id":"C1","round":0,"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","parent":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","note":"format_line_added","wins":27,"losses":16,"accepted":true,"dev_acc":0.8,"reference":{"prompt":"cf7e8a98a5cc","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C2","round":1,"prompt":"7583e9f4fcc9","parent":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1","note":"ok","wins":20,"losses":29,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.805,"reference":{"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C3","round":2,"prompt":"5b8ea6d3c681","parent":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1","note":"ok","wins":19,"losses":26,"accepted":false,"dev_acc":0.805,"reference":{"prompt":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1","pass":"current"}},{"id":"C4","round":3,"prompt":"9aba4803c8d3","parent":"1e7bee5b06e6","env":"E1","note":"format_line_added","wins":17